    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάγνυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>capable of
				being broken</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				385a14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θραυστὸν καὶ κ., ἀλλ᾽ οὐ θλαστόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HA</u>
					523b10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάγω</span>) <i>to be sunk</i> or <i>let
			down</i>, of a kind of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κότταβος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1244
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.667e
			</span></i>.</div>
